  "narrative": [
    "Management science is no longer a major or minor students can choose. Current students with a management science major or minor will be able to complete their degree; however, they will not be able to switch back into it if they decide to switch out.",
    "To graduate with a major, a minimum GPA of 2.0 is required in upper-division courses used to satisfy major requirements. All courses must be taken for a letter grade and passed with a grade of C– (C minus), or better, with the exception of ECON 195P, ECON 198, and ECON 199, for which P/NP grading is mandatory. No more than twelve units of ECON 195P, ECON 198, and ECON 199 taken P/NP may be counted toward major requirements. ECON 195P may only be taken twice for credit (eight units).",
    "The 100, 110, 120, 172, and 173 core courses are sequential. That is, A must be taken before B, and when applicable, B before C.",
    "To receive a bachelor of science degree in management science, no more than six upper-division courses taken externally from UC San Diego can be counted toward the major.",
    "Management science majors are strongly encouraged to take ECON 100A-B-C and ECON 120A-B-C in their sophomore year."
  ],
